<title>UK: NWE naphtha holds steady, but under pressure.</title>
<headline>NWE naphtha holds steady, but under pressure.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Naphtha stood its ground on Thursday in the face of heavy losses on screen crude.</p>
<p>July swaps were steady at $176.00 with august contagnoed by $1 or so and September by $1-2.</p>
<p>Dealers said there were several cargoes available with Russian and LVN around. A Russian cargo arriving July 10-20 was heard bid in the low $170s cif, but nothing was thought concluded.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
